        },
        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-1095",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.0 — Components · Author",
          "documentation": "Inside author.mjs. Everything here is transcription except the budgeter, and the budgeter is the reason this is code rather than a prompt: it is what stops a hold being a guess.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1096",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Trace reader",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs\n\nLoads the trace and refuses one without a beats array. Everything downstream is derived from this single file, which is what makes the .demo and the sidecar agree by construction rather than by care."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1097",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Speech-rate model",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs · CHARS_PER_SEC\n\nHow long a line takes to say, at 12.5 characters per second. The first value, 15.5, was derived by dividing text length by the gap between cues — which silently included the pause after each line, so it ran fast and under-estimated every clip. Back-solved from three real overlap warnings the true rate is 12.0-13.7; the constant sits at the slow end deliberately, because over-estimating costs one fewer line while under-estimating makes two lines talk over each other."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1098",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Narration budgeter",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs · budget()\n\nFits as many lines as the measured wait allows, spacing them so none overlaps the next, and stops at a ceiling because wall-to-wall talking over a 40s wait reads worse than a visible fast-forward. Lines that do not fit are returned as unused rather than dropped in silence, and an uncovered stretch over six seconds becomes a SPEEDS_MS range."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1099",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Selector registry",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs · ref()\n\nRuns once per step that touches an element and feeds both outputs from that one call: the name and intent go to the .demo selectors block, the spec and evidence to the sidecar. Neither file is written independently, so they cannot drift apart. A step names an element defined once in the trace's selectors table, and a name the table lacks is an error, not a guess."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1100",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Step emitter",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs · emitOne()\n\nOne DSL line per trace step: say, hold, wait, type, press, click, hover, park. A waitGone pulls in the budgeter and labels the number measured or ESTIMATED, because a figure a reader trusts as measured when it was guessed is worse than no figure. An ifAppears becomes a short-timeout guard for UI that only shows up sometimes."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1101",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Header writer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs\n\nWrites the provenance line, any hazards the walk recorded, the ready-to-paste SPEEDS_MS command, and the script headers from the trace: name, target, start, intro, outro, and intro-avatar and outro-avatar from its introAvatar and outroAvatar. Hazards go in the file rather than a chat log because that is where the next person will look."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1102",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Provenance stamper",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs\n\nTakes resolvedBy and the note from the trace instead of stamping them on. It used to hardcode claude-in-chrome, so a hand-authored trace produced a sidecar claiming it had been resolved live — the one lie that makes every other entry in the file untrustworthy."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1103",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
              "name": "Writer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs\n\nWrites the .demo and derives the sidecar path by swapping the extension — the same rule script.mjs uses to find it, which is why the two must sit together. Unused lines and SPEEDS_MS candidates are printed as notes for the person running it. --check compares instead of writing: a missing, stale or orphaned generated script fails, line endings ignored."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-1104",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1095"
              },
