                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: CUTS_MS, SPEEDS_MS · env\n\nTwo ways to shorten a take: a cut drops the frames, a speed keeps them and plays them fast. Reach for a speed first — a cut across an answer being written lands the viewer on a finished table having never seen it arrive. A reversed range, a factor at or below 1, or a cut overlapping a speed is rejected, because both cannot apply."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1821",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Time warp",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs\n\nThe single function that moves a timestamp. Ranges are applied partially when a timestamp falls inside one, which keeps a sped-up span in sync with itself rather than only at its far edge. No other stage does its own; that is what stops the picture and the voice drifting apart."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1822",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Frame selector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs\n\nDrops frames stamped earlier than the frame before them (they would push the picture behind the voice), drops frames inside a cut and rewrites the timestamp of the rest. Fewer than ten survivors is an error naming the cut rather than a two-frame video."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1823",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Gap reporter",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs\n\nPrints the five largest inter-frame gaps over a second. Those are exactly where the video freezes, so they are the candidates for the next cut."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1824",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Concat list writer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg concat demuxer\n\nA file and duration pair per frame, with the last frame repeated so its duration is honoured. Paths go in with forward slashes because the demuxer treats a backslash as an escape."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1825",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Encoder",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg libx264\n\nScales to 1920x1080 with lanczos at 60fps, CRF 18."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1826",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Telemetry mapper",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs\n\nNormalises pointer samples to 0..1 of the viewport, drops what fell inside a cut, and warps the rest. Nothing surviving is an error, because a silent empty cursor track is worse. The element boxes go through the same warp into highlights.json, a hover capped at HIGHLIGHT_HOLD_MS and a click ended at its release."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1827",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Cue mapper",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs\n\nThe identical filter and warp for narration cues, and it reports how many were dropped inside cuts. Doing this anywhere else silently desyncs the voiceover from the picture."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1828",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1819"
              },
              "name": "Auto-speed planner",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs · AUTO_SPEED\n\nTurns the driver's logged waits into speed ranges: every wait of at least AUTO_SPEED_MIN_MS with no narration over it, clipped to start after the previous line has finished and to end before the next begins, so speeding the picture can never pull two lines together. Line lengths come from the TTS clip cache, or the author's slow estimate before narration exists. Hand-written ranges win where they overlap."
            },
