        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-2580",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.7 — Components · Tightener",
          "documentation": "Inside tighten.mjs. The damage this stage can do is silent — a faded word or a dissolved zoom move still produces a clean file of a plausible length — so the placement rule is checked rather than trusted.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2581",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Options",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs\n\nmin, keep, speed, tail, xfade and the two detector floors. Every default errs toward leaving the video alone, because the failure mode here is squeezing too hard and that does not announce itself: the output is simply a video that feels rushed."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2582",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Detector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg freezedetect + silencedetect\n\nOne pass, both filters. It reports on stderr and exits 0, so the output is read from a spawn rather than a throwing exec. A run still open at the end of the file is closed at the duration rather than dropped, because that trailing run is the one that matters most."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2583",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Dead-run intersector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs\n\nDead means frozen AND silent. Either signal alone is wrong: a frozen screen under a narration line is the shot that line is playing over, and silence over a moving screen is a stretch that needs narrating, not cutting. Touching runs are merged so two detections do not become two seams."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2584",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Zoom guard",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs + {take}.recordly\n\nZoom windows are subtracted from the dead runs outright. A dead run butts right up against a zoom, because the zoom is triggered by a click and the screen goes still immediately after it, so a seam there dissolves the move and turns it into a snap."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2585",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Segment planner",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs\n\nLive stretches at 1x, dead ones at up to speed, never leaving less than keep of screen time. A run too short to hold a seam at each end, or one saving under 0.8s, is left alone: a seam is never free, and shaving 0.2s off a pause does not pay for one."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2586",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Placement check",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs\n\nRe-verifies every seam against the detected silence and the zoom list, and refuses to write if one is over either. Not belt and braces: a seam on a run edge fades a narration line up from nothing, and nothing catches that except watching the video."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2587",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Renderer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg xfade + acrossfade\n\nEach segment is trimmed and retimed, then dissolved into the next over a fade long enough to see. atempo only ever stretches silence, so the narration itself is never pitched or hurried."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2588",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
              "name": "Time map",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs + timemap.mjs\n\nWrites final-narrated-tight.mp4.timemap.json: each kept segment with its speed and where it starts in the output. Stages after tighten that place something at a moment of the take read it through timemap.mjs; the card renderer puts each section card where its beat opens its page (leadAtMs) once the previous line has ended, resumes the take when that open finished (leadEndMs), else cuts just before its beat line."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-2589",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2580"
              },
