        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-4093",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.13 — Components · Test Suites",
          "documentation": "Inside pipeline/test. Node built-in runner, so nothing extra to install. Neither suite calls a text-to-speech API, a browser or the app under demo, and fixtures are public: the committed example trace and media generated on the fly, never a private app files.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-4094",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-4093"
              },
              "name": "Unit suite",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: pipeline/test/unit · node:test\n\nPure functions, no ffmpeg and no network: voice and avatar selection in tts.mjs (on, off, typos, precedence, missing settings, with fetch stubbed), the .demo language in script.mjs, trace authoring and narration budgeting in author.mjs, and the colour helpers in brand.mjs. Every test clears the voice variables first, so a developer .env cannot change a result."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-4095",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-4093"
              },
              "name": "Integration suite",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: pipeline/test/integration · node:test\n\nThe real CLIs end to end. author.mjs to script.mjs to loading the scenario, in a temp folder, plus author.mjs --check on the committed traces; cards.mjs with the avatar on, off, with a clip missing and with a bad DEMO_AVATAR, checking durations, audio and pixels in the rendered cards. Skips itself where ffmpeg is missing."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-4096",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-4093"
              },
              "name": "Integration helpers",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: test/integration/helpers.mjs\n\nRuns a stage as its CLI with the voice and avatar variables cleared, makes solid-colour stand-in clips with a tone, and reads durations, audio streams and single pixels back out of a video."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-4097",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-4093"
              },
              "name": "Tests workflow",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: .github/workflows/tests.yml\n\nTwo jobs, unit and integration, on every pull request, push to main and merge group. Node 22 with npm ci in pipeline/; the integration job installs ffmpeg first."
            },
